WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.500
It's always seemed like Rob Dyrdek was living
the dream who wouldn't want to make millions

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.600
while competing in the sport they love and
goofing off with their friends?

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.360
But recently, he's stepped back from the spotlight.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.880
Here's what he's been up to, and why you won't
catch him on reality TV anymore.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:19.420
In September 2015, Dyrdek married his longtime
girlfriend Bryiana Flores.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.300
The two got engaged at Disneyland Resort in
April 2015.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.920
While they were watching the Aladdin Show,
Dyrdek secretly snuck around backstage and

00:00:27.939 --> 00:00:32.330
carried out a wild public proposal that could
have totally been a stunt on Rob Dyrdek's

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.300
Fantasy Factory.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:37.380
He came out on stage riding an elephant and
asked Flores to be his wife!

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:42.500
After enjoying a romantic and extravagant
"babymoon" in Bora Bora, the couple welcomed

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.060
their first child on September 9th, 2016:
a son named Kodah, according to E! News.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.640
Dyrdek was ecstatic about becoming a father
for the first time.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.940
In an Instagram post about his wife, he said,
in part,

00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.460
"As much as I love this woman with all of
my being, I could never express how proud

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:00.960
I am of how strong she is."

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:07.040
Dyrdek and Flores seem to be quite happy with
parenthood, and in December 2017, the couple

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:11.720
announced the arrival of their second child,
a baby girl named Nala, and expressed their

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.500
joy about giving Kodah a sibling and growing
their family.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.470
Now in his mid forties, Dyrdek waited until
later in life to start his family, but he

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.860
was ready for a change.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.580
Along with the announcement of the birth of
his daughter, he shared on Instagram,

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.600
"She is an angel from heaven.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.420
She is absolute perfection.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:29.420
She is our princess."

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:34.780
Dyrdek has admitted that he prefers to maintain
a stronger boundary between his business and

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:39.580
personal life now than he did in the past
and this change has been a long time coming.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.490
While Dyrdek was working on Rob &amp; Big, he
didn't like the lack of privacy that appearing

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.940
on MTV afforded him.

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.360
After the final season aired in 2008, MTV
originally approached Dyrdek with the prospect

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.780
of shooting an additional season, but Dyrdek
knew it was time for something different.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.340
He told ThoughtCO,

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.380
"My businesses were being affected, my skateboarding
was being affected, and I hated that it was

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.730
being filmed at my house.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.820
So, once we had a little break, it evolved.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.820
I thought, what if I added a skatepark to
my business?"

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.960
Thus, Rob Dyrdek's Fantasy Factory was born,
and Dyrdek could finally keep his home life

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.060
and his reality TV shenanigans separate.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:21.900
Dyrdek told Foundr that eventually working
in reality TV just took too much out of him.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:25.920
He wanted to put all that time toward his
other professional interests.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:30.720
He added that reality TV didn't give him the
same "return on energy" that building businesses

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.700
brought him, so he decided to switch up his
priorities.

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:38.980
He clearly isn't done with TV appearances
after all, Dyrdek has his show Ridiculousness.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:43.280
But when it comes to his involvement with
Ridiculousness, most of his responsibilities

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:48.350
center around discovering and curating hilarious
content for the show, which was inspired by

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:50.580
the format of America's Funniest Home Videos.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:55.900
Despite struggling to reconcile their differences
off-camera while filming the later seasons

00:02:55.910 --> 00:03:01.060
of Rob &amp; Big, Dyrdek and his co-star Christopher
"Big Black" Boykin always shared a strong

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.070
bond and years of happy memories.

00:03:03.380 --> 00:03:05.280
"My boy Big Black, welcome to our crib."

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.880
In 2017, Big Black shockingly passed away
after suffering a heart attack at the age

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:11.700
of 45.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.100
Naturally, Dyrdek was devastated, and he needed
time to grieve the loss.

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:20.630
The two had been inseparable for years, and
even after they decided that it was time to

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.680
close the door on Rob &amp; Big, Big Black still
made appearances on Fantasy Factory.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.640
Dyrdek shared his thoughts on the loss of
his friend on social media, tweeting,

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.200
"My heart is broken.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.100
I don't want [to] write this post.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.920
I don't want to believe that this is reality.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.620
I am so thankful for you."

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:41.940
Overall, it seems Dyrdek has allowed himself
to fade out of the spotlight by choice.

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:46.260
Although he has fun on the set of Ridiculousness,
he isn't looking to be the star of the show

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.840
anymore he'd rather be the guy pulling the
levers behind the curtain.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.340
He told Forbes,

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:55.770
"Anytime an opportunity presents itself, really
what I'm trying to do is put an infrastructure

00:03:55.770 --> 00:04:00.260
around me to creatively operate at a very
high level and be able to have the people

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.540
who can execute the idea.

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:05.040
I operate best on big vision and creative
detail."

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:10.680
Aside from hosting Ridiculousness, Dydek says
his true passion is for entrepreneurship,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:14.620
so he could also be the genius behind some
of your new favorite brands and products.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.660
Nowadays, he seems to be doing a little bit
of everything and he's loving it.

